cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BorderPulse, please cite it as below."
title: "BorderPulse: an open early-warning laboratory for the El Paso–Juárez Borderplex economy"
version: 6.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
authors:
  - family-names: Hunt
    given-names: Marcus
    email: marcusjhunt01@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A transparent, reproducible composite index of economic stress for the El Paso
  metropolitan area built from seven public monthly indicators (BLS LAUS/CES via FRED,
  Census trade, Federal Reserve exchange rates, Realtor.com housing), with a
  leakage-free back-test against pre-registered targets, episode-first inference with
  exact and bootstrap intervals, placebo and robustness tests, benchmark comparison
  against a local Sahm rule, a pre-registered onset evaluation and border-layer test,
  and a real-time vintage-audit framework.
keywords:
  - regional economics
  - early warning
  - El Paso
  - border economy
  - nowcasting
license: MIT
